Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.29,0:00:03.98,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,I'm glad I got a chance to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.98,0:00:08.53,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,Who knew the money moving around \Nthe crown princess was so fishy?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.53,0:00:12.11,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,I see why you're comptroller \Nof the treasury, assistant or not.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.39,0:00:17.73,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,Please, I'm in your debt for all \Nyou've been so good as to tell me.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.73,0:00:21.25,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,I hope I'll be seeing more\N of you, Rufus May.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.52,0:00:31.75,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Well?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.04,0:00:34.76,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,As you suspected, it would appear...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.76,0:00:37.04,Main - Top,Rufus,0,0,0,,Aldous Clayton is on his way \Nto interview her.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.59,0:00:41.15,Default,Maidservant A,0,0,0,,My mistress's room is \Nat the end of the hall.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.15,0:00:43.13,Default,Maidservant A,0,0,0,,I've made certain you'll have privacy.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.96,0:00:45.73,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,Aisha Huxley...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.93,0:00:51.40,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,What made her decide to confess \Na decade-old crime now?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.71,0:00:55.65,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,Oh, but she isn't the quarry\N you're after, is she...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.26,0:00:57.95,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,Deborah Darkian?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.87,0:01:05.88,Flashback - Italics,Maidservant A,0,0,0,,I've made certain you'll have privacy.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.25,0:01:11.73,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,Damn and blast!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.06,0:01:15.42,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,Hey, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.42,0:01:19.24,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,He took... the medicine bottle.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.24,0:01:21.78,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,Salvador of Daeg Gallus...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.17,0:01:24.17,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,She must mean that man.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.17,0:01:28.50,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,Sharon... Investigate my cousin Sharon...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.13,0:01:31.30,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,I will. Anything else?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.63,0:01:33.44,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,Scarlett...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.85,0:01:38.94,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,Do you think Scarlett will... forgive me?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.61,0:01:40.51,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,Sure she will.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.95,0:01:43.12,Default,Aisha,0,0,0,,Thank good—
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.11,0:01:57.22,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,A guard dog's disgrace is \Nhis owner's responsibility, no?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.22,0:02:00.47,Default,Servant A,0,0,0,,M-Murderer!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.22,0:02:02.73,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Goodbye...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.22,0:02:08.09,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Abigail O'Brian.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.53,0:03:43.00,Main - Top,Audrey,0,0,0,,What's a wanted murderer doing here?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.50,0:03:48.00,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,Somebody else killed her.\N I just got framed.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.00,0:03:50.76,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,What an unbelievably stupid dog you are!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.76,0:03:53.00,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,You could have at least \Nbeen smarter about it!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.40,0:03:55.50,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,I'm telling you, I didn't do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.77,0:03:57.63,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,Don't make excuses!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.63,0:04:00.50,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,That attitude is why you slip up,\N you mangy stray!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.45,0:04:03.01,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,Listen to me, you old hag!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.02,0:04:07.05,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,So, um, who might this be?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.05,0:04:11.02,Default,Rebekah,0,0,0,,That's Lady Audrey, our teacher.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.02,0:04:14.64,Default,Miriam,0,0,0,,She teaches us how to do \Nour makeup and pick out dresses.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.64,0:04:17.42,Default,Miriam,0,0,0,,And how to wrap gentlemen \Naround our fingers!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.42,0:04:18.84,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Wrap them...?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.84,0:04:21.03,Default,Miriam,0,0,0,,Oh, you're darling.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.03,0:04:23.52,Default,Rebekah,0,0,0,,It's all right if you don't understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.81,0:04:26.49,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,How long do you intend\N to sit around chattering?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.53,0:04:32.03,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,Why must everyone Abigail \Nbrings me be such utter...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.49,0:04:35.53,Default,Miriam,0,0,0,,What does Abby have to do with it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.54,0:04:42.21,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,I'll have you know the former Duke O'Brian\N charged me with guarding this place.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.21,0:04:44.80,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,I'll toss lazy layabouts out on their ear!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.70,0:04:54.06,Default,Rebekah,0,0,0,,Enough, silly.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.06,0:04:55.06,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.19,0:04:57.72,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,Look on the bottom right.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.80,0:05:02.00,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,This is Sharon Spencer, Aisha's cousin.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.58,0:05:05.10,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,It looks like she died on the same day.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.33,0:05:09.96,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,They say it was suicide, \Nbut I'll bet she was murdered.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.80,0:05:13.21,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Daeg Gallus again...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.21,0:05:15.06,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,They work fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.06,0:05:17.96,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,There must be some secret \Nthey really don't want to come out.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.47,0:05:19.52,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Pardon me.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.58,0:05:23.09,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Your Lordship?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.09,0:05:25.24,Default,Miriam,0,0,0,,My! Here to collect her again?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.89,0:05:27.74,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I need you to listen calmly.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.74,0:05:32.59,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Abigail has been arrested \Non suspicion of Aisha Huxley's murder.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.44,0:05:38.72,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,There was an anonymous tip.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.09,0:05:48.36,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,It said the fugitive Aldous Clayton is\Nnone other than Folkvangr's bouncer, Rudy,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.13,0:05:54.79,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,and that it was Abigail \Nwho provided him with his false identity.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.23,0:05:57.46,Flashback,Lucia,0,0,0,,Abby...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.09,0:06:04.13,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,She's therefore being investigated\Nfor masterminding Aisha's murder.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.38,0:06:08.16,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,B-But Lady Abigail had \Nnothing to do with Aisha!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.62,0:06:13.64,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Abigail wrote to Aisha a week ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.20,0:06:19.23,Flashback,Abigail,0,0,0,,I'll see to it that you receive\N an invitation from the Huxleys soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.25,0:06:22.78,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,This is my fault...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.24,0:06:26.36,Default,Miriam,0,0,0,,No, Connie. You did nothing wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.45,0:06:31.15,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I need to do something!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.33,0:06:33.90,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,I'll turn myself in.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.10,0:06:37.80,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,W-Wait a moment!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.80,0:06:38.49,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,Move!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.81,0:06:44.87,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I will not. Giving yourself up \Nwon't save Abby in your place.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.87,0:06:46.75,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,Then what am I supposed to do?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.02,0:06:49.33,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,We're going to think of something!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.33,0:06:51.48,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Right now! All of us together!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.26,0:06:57.56,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Connie.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.18,0:07:03.52,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,It {\i1}is{\i0} true that we have \Nour own way of doing things.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.52,0:07:05.17,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Do you have an idea?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.17,0:07:08.27,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,First, isn't there something \Nyou forgot to say?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.59,0:07:10.27,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Help me, Scarlett!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.42,0:07:14.27,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Oh, very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.62,0:07:16.34,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I shall save you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.48,0:07:21.20,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Naturally, since the charges are false,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.20,0:07:24.89,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,they have no evidence \Nto definitively prove Abigail's guilt.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.53,0:07:29.66,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Our enemies will send a judge \Nin their pocket for her trial.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.79,0:07:34.30,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Earl Kalvin Campbell \Nis set to try the case.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.59,0:07:37.10,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,In a word, he's a womanizer.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.68,0:07:41.88,Default,Kyle,0,0,0,,Your quintessential scumbag \Nwho's fathered children all over.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.30,0:07:46.07,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,A judge like that is bound \Nto have dirty secrets.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.07,0:07:47.22,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,So...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.68,0:07:52.45,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,We find out what they are first \Nand blackmail him ourselves!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.06,0:07:54.41,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Blackmail?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.41,0:07:56.15,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,In that case...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.49,0:08:02.16,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,call courtesans to the Earl John Doe Ball\N for some drunken merrymaking!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.16,0:08:08.27,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,Earl Campbell will leap at \Nthe novel entertainment! It's perfect!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.27,0:08:13.18,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,No one can think up \Ntasteless spectacles quite like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.77,0:08:15.33,Default,Rebekah,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.21,0:08:18.17,Default,Rebekah,0,0,0,,It's an interesting plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.50,0:08:20.66,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,Give the signal if the worst happens.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.67,0:08:23.67,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,I'll threaten him myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.94,0:08:28.15,Default,Miriam,0,0,0,,Thank you, Connie.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.15,0:08:30.80,Default,Miriam,0,0,0,,For giving us a chance to repay Abby.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.69,0:08:38.17,Default,Miriam,0,0,0,,Until a few years ago, Rebekah and I were \Nforced to work somewhere truly awful.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.84,0:08:41.07,Default,Miriam,0,0,0,,It was practically a prison.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.49,0:08:44.24,Default,Miriam,0,0,0,,Even if we'd escaped,\N we had nowhere to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.24,0:08:46.76,Default,Miriam,0,0,0,,They treated us like slaves.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.12,0:08:52.14,Default,Rebekah,0,0,0,,And then, along came Abby.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.42,0:08:58.18,Flashback,Abigail,0,0,0,,I've bought every girl in this place.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.73,0:09:00.80,Flashback,Abigail,0,0,0,,Now, let's get out of here.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.43,0:09:07.44,Default,Miriam,0,0,0,,That's how Abby rescued\N all of the girls working here.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.48,0:09:09.71,Default,Laura,0,0,0,,So...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.72,0:09:13.94,Default,Laura,0,0,0,,So, please, do whatever you can for her.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.93,0:09:18.69,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,O-Oh, please raise your heads.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.04,0:09:23.28,Default,Laura,0,0,0,,Go on now. Before Audrey catches on.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.28,0:09:24.95,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,Before who does what?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.31,0:09:30.47,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Why, Audrey...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.47,0:09:33.57,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,Planning how to get out \Nof work, are you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.57,0:09:36.20,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,I don't recall teaching you that!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.51,0:09:39.59,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,This is the problem with \Nthe lot of you Abigail brought in.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.59,0:09:41.63,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,You hardly pass for\N decent funeral flowers.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.63,0:09:44.09,Default,Miriam,0,0,0,,Abby isn't dead yet!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.09,0:09:46.44,Default,Miriam,0,0,0,,It's too soon for you to be so senile,\N you rotten old hag.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.44,0:09:49.73,Default,Rebekah,0,0,0,,"Rotten" is unfair. \NShe's a perfectly respectable old hag.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.73,0:09:50.93,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,Oh, am I?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.92,0:09:55.87,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,I see you girls are \Nas foul-mouthed as ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.48,0:09:58.69,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,Laura, go take down the sign.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.74,0:10:03.00,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,Don't we have a big party to attend?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.39,0:10:08.00,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,We'll close shop for tonight \Nand focus on cultivating new clientele.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.76,0:10:15.21,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,Go make yourselves up! All of you!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.03,0:10:20.51,Default,Miriam,0,0,0,,Audrey...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.51,0:10:24.77,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,What Abigail brings on herself \Nis no business of mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.77,0:10:30.01,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,But when they strike at her, \Nthey pick a fight with Folkvangr.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.46,0:10:32.65,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,Listen up, girls!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.76,0:10:39.39,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,Use every trick in the book\N to take this man for all he's worth.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.68,0:10:43.03,Default,Audrey,0,0,0,,Don't leave a solid bone in his body.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.97,0:10:53.24,Main - Italics,Kalvin {M},0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.71,0:10:57.25,Main - Italics,Kalvin {M},0,0,0,,I did my hair for today!\NI had my mask specially made!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.25,0:10:59.26,Main - Italics,Kalvin {M},0,0,0,,So why?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.04,0:11:04.55,Main - Italics,Kalvin {M},0,0,0,,Why doesn't anyone choose me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.55,0:11:07.88,Main - Italics,Kalvin {M},0,0,0,,That's...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.21,0:11:13.06,Main - Italics,Kalvin {M},0,0,0,,the pride of Folkvangr, \NMiriam the rose fairy!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.71,0:11:16.86,Default,Kalvin,0,0,0,,My lady.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.31,0:11:18.81,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,I beg your pardon.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.21,0:11:22.32,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,She's here with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.82,0:11:27.57,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,She simply won't have \Nanyone else. Excuse us.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.14,0:11:35.97,Main - Italics,Kalvin {M},0,0,0,,{\i0}I{\i1} lost to a man like {\i0}that{\i1}?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.99,0:11:39.04,Default,Kalvin,0,0,0,,Who are you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.34,0:11:42.35,Default,Rebekah,0,0,0,,M-My sincere apologies.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.34,0:11:45.95,Default,Kalvin,0,0,0,,Oh, dear me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.95,0:11:48.86,Default,Kalvin,0,0,0,,The beautiful moon has \Nshrouded herself in clouds.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.86,0:11:51.35,Default,Kalvin,0,0,0,,Has something happened to sadden you so?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.35,0:11:55.35,Default,Rebekah,0,0,0,,No. At least, nothing I'd dare\N to speak of here.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.35,0:11:59.85,Default,Kalvin,0,0,0,,Might I become the wind\N to blow your clouds away?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.95,0:12:05.86,Default,Rebekah,0,0,0,,Perhaps you've heard that the owner \Nof our establishment is under arrest.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.27,0:12:10.22,Default,Rebekah,0,0,0,,When I think that I may \Nend up on the street,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.22,0:12:12.74,Default,Rebekah,0,0,0,,I find myself overwhelmed with worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.74,0:12:15.34,Main - Italics,Kalvin {M},0,0,0,,Does she mean Abigail O'Brian?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.34,0:12:19.75,Main - Italics,Kalvin {M},0,0,0,,I thought it would be a boring job \Njust delivering a predetermined verdict,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.75,0:12:22.75,Main - Italics,Kalvin {M},0,0,0,,but what an unexpected perk.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.03,0:12:25.66,Default,Kalvin,0,0,0,,When that time comes, call on me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.14,0:12:31.76,Default,Kalvin,0,0,0,,I'm Kalvin Campbell. \NI promise you a comfortable life.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.42,0:12:38.14,Default,Rebekah,0,0,0,,To tell the truth, I've received \Na similar offer from Viscount Hamsworth.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.82,0:12:42.46,Default,Rebekah,0,0,0,,Please excuse me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.40,0:12:46.15,Default,Hamsworth,0,0,0,,It's quite true.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.15,0:12:48.15,Default,Miriam,0,0,0,,Oh, you beast.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.73,0:12:51.59,Default,Kalvin,0,0,0,,Wait! I'll double his offer!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.47,0:12:54.17,Default,Kalvin,0,0,0,,I have all the money you could want!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.17,0:12:55.66,Default,Kalvin,0,0,0,,It's true!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.42,0:12:59.45,Default,Rebekah,0,0,0,,And may I ask... where?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.05,0:13:02.55,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Ill-gotten funds?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.55,0:13:06.05,Default,Rebekah,0,0,0,,He operates hospitals \Nand orphanages, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.67,0:13:11.81,Default,Rebekah,0,0,0,,The country sponsors this, and he pockets\N some of the money on the sly.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.40,0:13:15.77,Flashback,Kalvin,0,0,0,,Don't worry! The money's clean on paper.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.77,0:13:21.75,Flashback,Kalvin,0,0,0,,I pool it in the secret accounts\Nof a citizen's group as "donations"!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.66,0:13:25.10,Default,Miriam,0,0,0,,We're lucky he's so loose-lipped.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.10,0:13:28.23,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,His tiny brain must be \Nas loose as his pants.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.63,0:13:32.12,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,So, um, what citizens' group is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.12,0:13:34.63,Default,Rebekah,0,0,0,,It's called the Violet Association.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.65,0:13:37.93,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,My, what a coincidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.38,0:13:43.75,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,O-Oh! That woman all in pink is...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.75,0:13:46.71,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Kimberly Smith of the Violet Association.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.50,0:13:52.45,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,And who might you be \Nto take me aside so abruptly?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.45,0:13:54.65,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I am called "Miss C."
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.65,0:13:57.64,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,Oh, goodness me. What can I do for you?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.06,0:14:01.72,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What is your relationship \Nwith Earl Kalvin Campbell?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.72,0:14:04.65,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,The earl? He's a magnificent gentleman.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.94,0:14:09.66,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,He sympathizes with our cause \Ndespite his aristocratic origins.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.66,0:14:11.90,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,And donates to it?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.90,0:14:15.91,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,How grim you look. \NDonating to a cause is hardly a crime.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.19,0:14:20.63,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Indeed, unless the money \Nwas obtained illegally.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.63,0:14:22.17,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.73,0:14:24.92,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I hear your association \Nkeeps secret accounts.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.62,0:14:29.00,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I take it she genuinely \Ndoesn't know about them.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.00,0:14:30.33,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,Tell me,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.69,0:14:32.92,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,did the earl tell you that?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.68,0:14:40.49,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,I see. The rat is probably... \Nin our youth committee, I suppose.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.49,0:14:44.46,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,How dare he use a defenseless \Ncitizens' group as cover.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.16,0:14:48.70,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,That Campbell boy has nerve, \NI'll give him that.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.32,0:14:50.70,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,By the by,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.70,0:14:54.70,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,I suppose you plan to blackmail him \Ninto acquitting Abigail?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.95,0:15:01.21,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,To think a "sincere" Grail \Nwould fight fire with fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.21,0:15:03.95,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,Well, I can't say it's a bad plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.95,0:15:07.00,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,But you're not quite up to the task.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.20,0:15:12.12,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,Very well. I owe you for telling me \Nabout the secret accounts,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.12,0:15:14.23,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,so let me take it from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.23,0:15:16.60,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.60,0:15:20.98,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,We don't want to see the O'Brians \Noverthrown any more than you do.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.98,0:15:27.61,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,We didn't spend ten years weakening the \NDarkians only to watch them rise again.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.91,0:15:29.27,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,Just who is this woman?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.31,0:15:35.37,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,You can't trust me? \NThen I'll give you a little hint.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.81,0:15:38.65,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,What color are violets?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.54,0:15:46.13,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,Our country's violets \Nhave an unusual reddish hue.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.56,0:15:52.64,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,It has come to represent the royal family \Nbecause it matches their eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.63,0:15:57.18,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,The royals of Faris, on the other hand, \Nhave bluish-purple eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.14,0:16:02.43,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,In both Adelbide and Faris, \Nthese eye colors symbolize their royalty.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.25,0:16:06.70,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,Which would suggest the Violet Association\Nthat Kimberly belongs to is...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.70,0:16:08.34,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,What are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.32,0:16:11.28,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,It's almost time for the verdict.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.67,0:16:13.56,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Do you think she'll be all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.56,0:16:15.80,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,That depends on Kimberly Smith.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.20,0:16:27.76,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Lady Abigail...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.76,0:16:28.85,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Miss Grail?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.77,0:16:33.04,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Your Lordship!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.42,0:16:36.54,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,How did it go? \NWhat was the verdict?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.89,0:16:37.98,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.05,0:16:42.31,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Due to insufficient evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.31,0:16:43.55,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Although...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.02,0:16:48.85,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,the earl looked as if {\i1}he'd{\i0} been \Nsentenced to death when he delivered it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.28,0:16:51.73,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,It seems that woman managed well enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.37,0:16:56.41,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Abigail will be released as soon \Nas the formalities are taken care of.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.41,0:16:59.41,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Th-Thank goodness!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.83,0:17:03.16,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,Oh no. I feel faint.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.41,0:17:10.53,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.44,0:17:12.89,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,So close...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.68,0:17:15.78,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,He's so, so, so close!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.78,0:17:18.06,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,Oh, his chest sure is firm...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.06,0:17:21.86,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,Wait, no! I mean, this is... I know! \NThis is a kind of a rescue effort!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.86,0:17:24.03,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,Certainly not a lover's embrace or...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.69,0:17:28.30,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Your face is flushed.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.64,0:17:30.15,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Do you have a fever or—
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.15,0:17:34.23,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,N-N-Not at all! I'm quite well!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.23,0:17:36.42,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Yes, yes. That's enough of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.29,0:17:47.57,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,Abby!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.67,0:17:52.54,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,I... wasn't the least bit worried for you!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.14,0:17:54.45,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,Lucia...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.20,0:18:06.32,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,After that...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.94,0:18:10.82,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,once news of Lady Abigail's \Ninnocence spread,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.33,0:18:14.57,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,the search for the true culprit\N led to the arrest of a suitable man,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.92,0:18:18.46,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,who confessed to Aisha's murder\Nand took his own life that evening.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.13,0:18:21.33,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,Meanwhile,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.69,0:18:23.55,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,an accusation started doing the rounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.48,0:18:28.93,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,It claimed someone had leaked information\Nabout Aisha which had to her murder.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.69,0:18:30.75,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,And that someone...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.91,0:18:34.75,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,was Amelia Hobbes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.09,0:18:42.02,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,Crown Princess Cecilia!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.59,0:18:46.35,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Who're you? And who are you \Ncalling "crown princess"?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.59,0:18:49.10,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,You can't fool me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.42,0:18:53.80,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,Word has spread, and no publisher \Nwill give me the time of day now!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.80,0:18:58.61,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,To make my comeback, \NI need a scandal that no one can deny!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.18,0:19:01.37,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,You need {\i1}what{\i0}?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.72,0:19:02.86,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,Cici.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.92,0:19:09.10,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,Almost every other child \Nin your old orphanage died in a fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.10,0:19:11.47,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,Only two remain unaccounted for.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.47,0:19:13.63,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,You and that boy, Cici—
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.33,0:19:20.38,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Cici is dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.14,0:19:24.20,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Do you want to die too?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.39,0:19:32.65,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Then disappear from this country\N before the day is out.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.94,0:19:34.41,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,If you don't,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.41,0:19:39.09,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,I'll dye that shabby red hair \Nof yours a lovely crimson.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.43,0:19:49.14,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,What are you racking \Nyour inadequate brain over?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.14,0:19:50.21,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You're awful!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.21,0:19:52.45,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I've told you, your face gives you away.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.44,0:19:56.71,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Remember what Abigail said?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.12,0:19:59.83,Flashback,Abigail,0,0,0,,Connie, you'd better watch out yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.83,0:20:04.78,Flashback,Abigail,0,0,0,,This was too smoothly done to be\N a cover-up of a decade-old crime.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.78,0:20:09.04,Flashback,Abigail,0,0,0,,Something tells me there's yet \Na big secret we don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.71,0:20:12.89,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Daeg Gallus is hunting \Nfor Lady Lily's key.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.09,0:20:18.83,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,So if we solve the mystery of that key \Nand the phrase "the Holy Grail of Eris,"
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.75,0:20:22.38,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,it may give us a clue.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.38,0:20:23.49,Default,San,0,0,0,,Hello there,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.49,0:20:25.59,Default,San,0,0,0,,charming young lady.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.24,0:20:32.50,Default,San,0,0,0,,I'm looking for the Grand Merillian. \NMight I ask you the way?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.50,0:20:35.11,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,O-Of course. It's just—
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.11,0:20:35.99,Default,Eularia,0,0,0,,San!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.99,0:20:38.41,Default,San,0,0,0,,Oh, Eularia.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.74,0:20:43.52,Default,Eularia,0,0,0,,I looked everywhere for you! Honestly! \NYou lose your way at the drop of a hat!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.52,0:20:48.01,Default,San,0,0,0,,Me? Surely it was you who lost your way.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.28,0:20:52.18,Default,Eularia,0,0,0,,Yes, yes. I'm sure that's \Nhow it seems to {\i1}you{\i0}!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.18,0:20:55.01,Default,Eularia,0,0,0,,Now, please, at least carry a map.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.86,0:20:57.03,Default,Eularia,0,0,0,,See this?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.30,0:21:00.28,Default,Eularia,0,0,0,,You take the letters \Nand number written here
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.28,0:21:02.23,Default,Eularia,0,0,0,,and use them to...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.23,0:21:05.14,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,That's a large bundle on her back.\N What could it be?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.76,0:21:09.04,Default,San,0,0,0,,I see. That does seem convenient.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.04,0:21:11.92,Default,Eularia,0,0,0,,Doesn't it just? \NNow you won't get lost any—
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.92,0:21:13.44,Default,San,0,0,0,,Here. For you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.41,0:21:16.81,Default,San,0,0,0,,I never get lost, you see.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.81,0:21:18.42,Default,Eularia,0,0,0,,I beg your pardon?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.72,0:21:21.92,Default,San,0,0,0,,I'm San. May I ask your name?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.20,0:21:24.66,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I'm C-Constance Grail.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.66,0:21:27.92,Default,San,0,0,0,,Grail? Why...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.92,0:21:29.76,Default,San,0,0,0,,What a lovely name.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.76,0:21:32.42,Default,Eularia,0,0,0,,W-Wait for me, San!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.42,0:21:34.43,Default,Eularia,0,0,0,,Listen until I'm done talking to you!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.87,0:21:36.44,Default,Eularia,0,0,0,,Honestly! Why must you always...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.43,0:21:42.58,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Lady Lily's key!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.58,0:21:44.70,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,This is no key.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.36,0:21:48.71,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I tracked down where it was made.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.71,0:21:51.81,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,It's merely a key-shaped decoration.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.81,0:21:52.70,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,However,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.06,0:21:57.20,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,this inscription was added\N at Lily's express direction.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.20,0:22:00.70,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,P10E3...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.11,0:22:04.20,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.22,0:22:06.92,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Excuse me for a moment!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.29,0:22:10.36,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,What's come over you?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.43,0:22:12.85,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Scarlett...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.47,0:22:16.71,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I think I might have figured it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.07,0:22:28.12,Default,Credits,0,0,0,,{\\fad(480,524)\fs12\fnArial\c&H351F51&\3c&H9985A7&\blur1\shad0\pos(494,284.666)}Translation:\h\h\h\h\h\h\hWilliam Varteresian
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.76,0:22:33.83,Default,Credits,0,0,0,,{\an8\fad(500,520)\fs10\fnArial\c&H351F51&\3c&H9985A7&\blur1\shad0\pos(160,237.667)}Subtitle Timing:\N{\fs12}Edgar Cruz\N\N\N{\fs10}Subtitle Editing:\N{\fs12}Riley Dalton
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.89,0:22:38.96,Default,Credits,0,0,0,,{\an8\fad(500,520)\fs10\fnArial\c&H351F51&\3c&H9985A7&\blur1\shad0\pos(160,254)}Quality Check:\N{\fs12}SMR\N\N\N{\fs10}Translation Check:\N{\fs12}Sriram Gurunathan
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.98,0:22:22.06,Signs,Signs; title,0,0,0,,A BANQUET OF INSECTIVOROUS PLANTS
